  "body": "Requested by the user (2026-11-11), who has a fixture **subplate for the Tormach microARC 4** 4th axis.\n\n**What:** a generic **rotary subplate**: a fixture plate mounted on the 4th axis (faceplate or chuck), turning with A, so parts or vises bolted to it are indexed.\n- A plate on the A axis, with a grid and dowel pattern like the sibling fixture-plate issue, and parameters for size, thickness and offset from the A centerline.\n- It **turns with the work:** it's included in the A-index swing check (#804/PR #810: tagged fixtures that turn with the work count in the swept radius) and judged in each indexed pose by the existing posed fixture laws (#339 slice 3).\n- Fixtures placed on it snap to its grid and turn with it.\n\nEffort: high (it rides the rotary and the swing check).\n\n**Done means:**\n- A subplate can be mounted on the microARC A with fixtures on it, turning with every index.\n- The swing check counts it.\n- Collisions are judged in each pose.\n- Pinned. **Checked on the user's microARC subplate.**\n\nDepends on #819 (fixture plates) and on #785/#804 (microARC A, PRs #798/#810). Part of #339.\n",
